HINT LOST: the PV behind this claim is gone: oc get pv, check the backend volume; restore from snapshot or recreate, never delete the claim first
HINT NOPV: this claim needs a pre-created PV (empty class or no-provisioner): oc get pv, match size, access mode and class, or create one
HINT UNKNOWNSC: the named StorageClass does not exist: oc get sc, fix the typo in the claim or create the class
HINT SELECTEDSTUCK: the scheduler picked a node but the provisioner could not create the volume there: oc describe pvc (ProvisioningFailed), check zone and topology of that node
HINT PROVISIONFAILED: Immediate class, dynamic provisioner, still Pending: oc describe pvc for ProvisioningFailed, check the CSI controller pods and quota on the backend
HINT MULTIDEFAULT: more than one default StorageClass: claims without a class get an arbitrary one; keep exactly one default
HINT LOCALIMMEDIATE: a no-provisioner class bound Immediate binds before scheduling and strands pods: use volumeBindingMode WaitForFirstConsumer
HINT WAITFORCONSUMER: not a fault: the claim stays Pending until a pod that uses it is scheduled; if no pod exists yet, this is expected
RESULT CRIT crit=6 warn=3 info=1 pvcs=10 healthy=3
